## 📝 Section 7: Git Workflow

**Optimized Pattern:** Clear branching strategy, Conventional Commits, and pre-commit hooks that never get bypassed.

```markdown
## Git Workflow

**See `/docs/git-workflow.md` for complete workflow and conventions.**

### Branching
- **Pattern:** `feature/<description>`, `fix/<description>`, `chore/<description>`
- **Strategy:** [Feature branches, trunk-based development, git-flow, etc.]
- **Protected branches:** [main, master, production, etc.]
- **Merge strategy:** [Squash and merge, merge commits, rebase, etc.]

### Commit Conventions

Use **Conventional Commits** format **with user story reference**:

```
<type>: <subject>

[optional body]

Implements: docs/features/<user-story-file>.md

[optional footer]
```

**Types:** feat, fix, chore, test, refactor, docs, style, perf

**REQUIRED for user story commits:**
- Include `Implements: docs/features/us-XXX-<story-name>.md` in commit footer
- Use exact filename from `/docs/features/`
- Place before other footers (e.g., Claude Code attribution)
- For multiple stories, list all files

**Examples:**
```
feat: add user authentication flow

- Implement login/register pages
- Add JWT token handling
- Tests: 85% coverage

Implements: docs/features/us-001-client-registration-auth.md

 
Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
```

```
fix: correct validation in signup form

Implements: docs/features/us-001-client-registration-auth.md
```

```
chore: bump dependencies to latest versions

# No "Implements" line needed for chores not tied to user stories
```

**Why This Matters:**
- Provides traceability between code changes and requirements
- Required for updating `docs/high-level-user-stories.md`
- Makes code review easier (reviewers can check against acceptance criteria)

### Pre-Commit Hooks

✅ Configured (runs automatically on every commit):
- [Linter] --fix (e.g., ESLint, Pylint, Ruff)
- [Formatter] --write (e.g., Prettier, Black)
- Type checking (e.g., TypeScript, mypy)
- Tests (unit tests, fast subset, or affected tests)
- Build check (verify production build succeeds)
- Commit message validation

**⚠️ CRITICAL:**
- **NEVER** use `--no-verify` to bypass hooks
- Fix issues before committing
- Only bypass if explicitly requested by user
- If tests/build are too slow for pre-commit, run in CI instead
